hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22194","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad al-A'raj, from a man, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man approaching his wife in her anus."
"22195","Isma'il narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: The traveler wipes over the socks three nights, and the resident a day and a night."
"22196","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Ibn Mahdi both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning wiping over the socks: A day and a night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler."
"22197","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymi narrating from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Three days, Shu'bah said: I think he said: and their nights, for the traveler concerning wiping over the socks."
"22198","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Harami ibn Abdillah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Absi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backsides."
"22199","Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Harami ibn Abdillah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, likewise."
"22200","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Khuzaymah, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned cleaning, and said: Three stones with no dung in them."
"22201","Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Taymi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wipe over the khuffs for three days, and had we asked him for more he would have given us more."
"22202","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Umara ibn Khuzayma, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their back passages."
"22203","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, he heard him narrating from Khuzayma ibn Thabit: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about wiping over the khuffs, and he permitted the traveler three days and their nights, and the resident a day and a night. Abdullah said: My father said: I heard it from Sufyan twice, mentioning for the resident, and had the questioner elaborated in his question he would have given them more."
"22204","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Malik and Khuzayma ibn Thabit and Usama ibn Zayd, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The plague is a filth or a punishment with which a people were punished; if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not enter upon it."
"22205","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Abu Khuzayma, from Umara ibn Khuzayma, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about istinja: Three stones among which there is no dung."
"22206","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hammad and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed for the traveler three, and for the resident a day and a night."
"22207","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Madini, meaning al-Khatmi, narrated to me, he said: I heard Umara ibn Uthman ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrating from Khuzayma ibn Thabit that he saw in his dream that he was kissing the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of that, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, handed him to him, so he kissed his forehead."
"22208","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Khatmi informed us, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that his father said: I saw in a dream that I was prostrating upon the forehead of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of that, and he said: The spirit does not meet the spirit, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inclined his head like this, and he placed his forehead upon the forehead of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22209","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, they said: Hassan, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Sahl, narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Ali, from Harami ibn Amr al-Khatmi, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their back passages."
"22210","Rawh narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever commits a sin and the hadd of that sin is carried out upon him, it is his expiation."
"22211","Al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us that he heard Urwa narrating from Umara ibn Khuzayma al-Ansari, narrating from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan comes to a man and says: Who created the heavens? And he says: Allah. Then he says: Who created the earth? And he says: Allah. Until he says: Who created Allah? So if one of you finds that, let him say: I have believed in Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22212","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about wiping over the khuffs, he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"22213","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22214","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the like of it."
"22215","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Sufyan, and Abu Nuaym said: Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed for the traveler three, and for the resident a day and a night. He said: By Allah, had the questioner continued in his question, he would have made it five. And Abu Nuaym said: A day for the resident."
"22216","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, Amr ibn Khuzayma narrated to me, from Umara ibn Khuzayma, from his father Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about cleaning after relieving oneself, and he said: Three stones among which there is no dung."
"22217","Yunus and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, he said: My grandfather kept withholding his weapon on the Day of the Camel until Ammar was killed at Siffin, then he drew his sword and fought until he was killed. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The transgressing party will kill Ammar."
"22218","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usama ibn al-Had that Ubayd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Waili narrated to him that Harami ibn Abd Allah al-Waqifi narrated to him that Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Khatmi narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is not shy of the truth, three times: Do not approach women in their posteriors."
"22219","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Hakam and Hammad informed me, they heard Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he permitted three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"22220","Rawh narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever commits a sin and the hadd of that sin is carried out upon him, it is his expiation."
"22221","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah al-Dastuwa'i narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Abu Masud Uqba ibn Amr al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr at the beginning of the night, its middle, and its end."
"22222","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Khatmi informed us, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that his father said: I saw in a dream as if I were prostrating upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of that, and he said: The spirit does not meet the spirit, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inclined his head like this, and he placed his forehead upon the forehead of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22223","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said about istinja: Can not one of you find three stones?"
"22224","He said: And a man informed me, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, he said, upon him be peace: Three stones among which there is no dung."
"22225","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"22226","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, my father narrated to me, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident. By Allah, had the questioner continued in his question, he would have made it five."
"22227","Uthman ibn Umar, he is Ibn Faris, narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, the possessor of the two testimonies, from his uncle, that Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari saw in a dream that he prostrated upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he informed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of that, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lay down for him and said: Fulfill your dream with that, so he prostrated upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22228","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Umara ibn Khuzayma al-Ansari narrated to me that his uncle narrated to him, and he was from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought a horse from a Bedouin, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had him follow him to pay him the price of his horse. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened walking and the Bedouin lagged, and men began intercepting the Bedouin and bargaining for the horse, not knowing that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had bought it, until some of them offered the Bedouin more in bargaining than the price of the horse for which the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had bought it. The Bedouin called to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: If you are buying this horse then buy it, otherwise I will sell it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped when he heard the call of the Bedouin and said: Did I not buy it from you? The Bedouin said: No, by Allah, I did not sell you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, indeed I bought it from you. The people began gathering around the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Bedouin while they disputed, and the Bedouin kept saying: Bring a witness who testifies that I sold you. Whoever came from the Muslims said to the Bedouin: Woe to you, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say nothing but the truth. Until Khuzayma came and listened to the exchange of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the exchange of the Bedouin, and the Bedouin kept saying: Bring a witness who testifies that I sold you. Khuzayma said: I testify that you sold him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to Khuzayma and said: On what basis do you testify? He said: By believing you, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made the testimony of Khuzayma the testimony of two men."
"22229","Sakan ibn Nafi Abu al-Hasan al-Bahili narrated to us, Salih, meaning Ibn Abi al-Akhdar, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Umara ibn Khuzayma informed me that Khuzayma saw in a dream that he was prostrating upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So Khuzayma came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lay down, then said to him: Fulfill your dream, so he prostrated upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22230","Amir ibn Salih al-Zubayri narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, and Khuzayma is the one whose testimony the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made the testimony of two men. Ibn Shihab said: Umara ibn Khuzayma informed me from his uncle, and he was from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Khuzayma ibn Thabit saw in sleep that he was prostrating upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lay down for him, so he prostrated upon his forehead."
